which one of the following?','{"A":"Gamma globulin infusion.","B":"Platelet transfusion.","C":"Plasma infusion.","D":"Corticosteroids.","E":"Azathioprine."}','D','Initial therapy for bleeding tendency in ITP in adults is with corticosteroids. Corticosteroids are thought to reduce the clearance of platelets from the circulation.
(Option A) Intravenous gamma globulin infusion is indicated if there is inadequate response to high-dose corticosteroids.
(Option B) Since platelets are rapidly cleared from the blood in ITP, platelet transfusion is of little benefit in long-term management of the disease. However, it may be considered for life-threatening significant bleeding or prior to emergency
splenectomy.
((Opion E) Azathioprine is not used as initial therapy, but may be considered as a corticosteroid-sparing agent for long-term management.
