tion (10-15 minutes), no requirement to check a patient’s blood group, minimal risk of viral transmission due to pathogen reduction and inactivation steps during manufacturing, and reduced risk of other clinical\nadverse reactions such as transfusion-associated circulatory overload or transfusion-associated acute lung injury.\nProthrombinex-VF, a three-factor PCC, is the only product currently in routine use in Australia and New Zealand for warfarin reversal. Despite instructions by the Warfarin Reversal Consensus Guidelines published in 2004 recommended that it be\nsupplemented with FFP, there have been several reports of successful use of Prothrombinex-VF without addition of FFP. Prothrombinex-VF has been used successfully to electively reverse anticoagulation in patients on warfarin therapy with a stable\nINR, and achieved the target INR in over 90% of patients. However, since the efficacy of Prothrombinex-VF alone has not been extensively evaluated for patient with major or life-threatening bleeding or INR > 10, current recommendation is that\nProthrombinex-VF is supplemented with FFP for addition of adequate amounts of factor VII to ensure optimal reversal of the anticoagulant effect of warfarin when major or life-threatening bleeding is a concern.\nFor life-threatening (critical organ) and clinically significant bleeds, the consensus is to use the maximum dose of Prothrombinex-F (with vitamin K1 and FFP) and the maximum amount of FFP when Prothrombinex-VF is unavailable.\n \nRecommendations for managing patients on warfarin therapy with bleeding are summarized in the following table:\nClinical setting\nRecommendations\nINR ≥1.5 with life-threatening (critical organ) bleeding\n1. Stop warfarin therapy AND give:\n2. Vitamin K (5-10mg IV) AND\n3. Prothrombinex-VF (50IU/kg IV) AND\n4. FFP (150-300ml)\nIf Prothrombinex-VF unavailable, give FFP (15ml/kg)\nINR≥2 with clinically significant bleeding (not life-threatening)\n1. Stop warfarin therapy AND give:\n2. Vitamin K (5-10mg IV) AND\n3. Prothrombinex-VF (35-50IU/kg IV)\nIf Prothrombinex-VF unavailable, give FFP (15ml/kg)\nAny INR with minor bleeding\nOmit warfarin, repeat INR the following day and adjust the warfarin dose to maintain INR within the therapeutic range\nIf bleeding risk is high or INR>4.5 give vitamin K (1-2mg orally or 0.5-1mg IV)\n \nRecommendations for managing patients on warfarin therapy with a high INR but no bleeding are summarized in the following table:\nClinical setting\nRecommendations\nINR above the therapeutic range but <4.5 and no bleeding\nLower or omit the next dose of warfarin\nResume therapy at a lower warfarin dose when INR approaches the therapeutic INR","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","anticoag","dose","guideline","management","therapy","treatment","warfarin"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"4eb7dc2c07a56a6c293c40ec9eac407d04247246","duplicate_group_id":"exact-4eb7dc2c07a5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6800ad18f5bab7bd41e7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":611,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
