If INR>1.5 - defer surgery or if urgent administer Prothrombinex-VF (use FFP if
Prothrombinex-VF unavailable)
For urgent surgery, check INR before surgery and administer Prothrombinex-VF before
surgery. Use FFP if Prothrombinex unavailable.
Recommence warfarin on the night of surgery at the previous maintenance dose.
 
Consider bleeding risk against thrombosis
If using LMWH, begin with prophylaxis dose; if UFH is used avoid bolus dose and aim to prolong the aPTT
by 1.5 times.
Delay resumption of therapeutic dose of LMWH for 48-72 hours after surgery in the absence of bleeding
Continue LMWH or UFH for a minimum of 5 days and cease 48 hours after target INR is reached.
In surgery with high bleeding risk, consider using prophylactic dose LMWH or UFH only and cease 48 hours
after target INR is reached.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-91c1008a9374","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ac0876195163698aabec","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":619,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"ac0876195163698aabec","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":619,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 56-year-old woman is brought to the emergency department with sudden-onset severe epigastric pain. On examination, she has a blood pressure of 90/55mmHg, heart rate of 110bpm, and respiratory rate of 22 breaths per minute. There is\nabdominal guarding and rigidity, as well as marked tenderness and rebound tenderness over the epigastric area. A chest X-ray reveals free air under the right hemi-diaphragm. Based on clinical findings, a perforated peptic ulcer is diagnosed and the\npatient is planned for emergency laparotomy. She is on warfarin due to deep vein thrombosis (DVT) that developed 2 weeks ago. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"Stop warfarin, give vitamin K and do the surgery.","B":"Proceed with the surgery.","C":"Give fresh frozen plasma (FFP) and proceed with the surgery.","D":"Add intravenous heparin and perform the surgery.","E":"Stop warfarin, give her heparin and proceed with the surgery."},"source_answer":"C","source_explanation":"This patient is in need of emergency life-saving surgery in the setting of perforated peptic ulcer disease and clinical manifestation of peritonitis (abdominal rigidity and guarding). In the event of need for life-saving or emergency surgeries where\ndeferring the surgery is not possible, warfarin effect should be reversed immediately using prothrombin complex concentrate (CCP) (Prothrombinex-VF®), or fresh frozen plasma (FFP) if CCP unavailable, regardless of the risk of potential VTE if\nwarfarin is temporarily stopped. Any option offering addition of vitamin K to cessation of warfarin and administration of CCP (or FFP) woudl be the most appropraite management (not an option).\n(Option A) Cessation of warfarin and administration of vitamin K was the method of choice if the patient had an INR of 2-3 within the past 2-4 weeks and there was a time window for deferral of the surgery for at least 24 hours. In such cases, vitamin\nK is given intravenously the evening before the surgery and INR is checked on the day of the surgery. An INR of ≤1.5 is safe to proceed with the surgery. If INR is >1.5 Prothrombinex-VF® should be given (FFP is used if Prothrombinex-VF is not\navailable)\n(Option B) Proceeding with the surgery without warfarin reversal is associated with significant risk of intra- or post-operative bleeding and not recommended.\n(Option D) Addition of heparin adds to the risk of bleeding.\n(Option E) Cessation of warfarin and bridging with heparin is indicated in patients with high risk of VTE, who are planned for elective surgery. The protocol is not used for emergency procedures.\n \nTOPIC REVIEW\nManagement of patients on warfarin therapy who are undergoing an invasive procedure is according to the following table:\nRisk\nBefore surgery\nAfter surgery\nLow\nWithhold warfarin 4-5 days before surgery\nCheck INR the day before surgery; if INR is 2-3 administer 3mg vitamin K IV\nDay of surgery:\nINR≤1.5 – surgery can proceed\nINR>1.5 – defer surgery or if urgent administer Prothrombinex-VF (use FFP if\nProthrombinex-VF unavailable)\nConsider preoperative VTE prophylaxis using LMWH if immobilized\nFor procedures with low risk of bleeding (e.g. cataract, dental, dermatological) continue\nwarfarin\nRecommence warfarin on the night of surgery at the previous maintenance dose.\nConsider VTE prophylaxis as per local guidelines\nHigh\nOPTION 1\nWithhold warfarin 4-5 days before surgery\nOnce INR<2 start LMWH e.g. 1.5mg daily or 1mg twice a day , OR unfractionated heparin\n(UFH) infusion\nIf LMWH is used, the last dose should be 24 hours before surgery \nIf UFH is used, stop infusion 4-6hours before surgery\nOPTION 2\nIf INR has been stable within 2-3 in the past 2-4 weeks administer vitamin K, 3mg IV the day\nbefore surgery\nDay of surgery:\nIf INR≤1.5 - surgery can proceed\nIf INR>1.5 - defer surgery or if urgent administer Prothrombinex-VF (use FFP if\nProthrombinex-VF unavailable)\nFor urgent surgery, check INR before surgery and administer Prothrombinex-VF before\nsurgery. Use FFP if Prothrombinex unavailable.\nRecommence warfarin on the night of surgery at the previous maintenance dose.\n \nConsider bleeding risk against thrombosis\nIf using LMWH, begin with prophylaxis dose; if UFH is used avoid bolus dose and aim to prolong the aPTT\nby 1.5 times.\nDelay resumption of therapeutic dose of LMWH for 48-72 hours after surgery in the absence of bleeding\nContinue LMWH or UFH for a minimum of 5 days and cease 48 hours after target INR is reached.\nIn surgery with high bleeding risk, consider using prophylactic dose LMWH or UFH only and cease 48 hours\nafter target INR is reached.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","dose","guideline","management","prophyl","therapy","warfarin"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"91c1008a9374437dc57b58989b0f5dc1ea6a9f18","duplicate_group_id":"exact-91c1008a9374","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ac0876195163698aabec","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":619,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
