antiphospholipid syndrome. She is currently on aspirin. Which one of the following would be the next best step in management?','{"A":"Do nothing, as aspirin alone is adequate.","B":"Start her on prophylactic dose of low molecular weight heparin.","C":"Start her on warfarin.","D":"Start her on therapeutic dose of low molecular weight heparin","E":"Arrange for elective abortion."}','B','For women with laboratory-proven criteria for antiphospholipid antibody syndrome and one or more miscarriages after 10 weeks gestation, combined therapy with low-dose aspirin (50 to 100 mg per day) and prophylactic dose of low molecular
weight heparin (LMWH) upon confirmation of intrauterine pregnancy is recommended. Therefore, addition of low-molecule weight heparin (LMWH) in prophylactic dose would be the next best step in management. Treatment should be continued
throughout the pregnancy. Therapy is withheld at the time of delivery and is restarted after delivery, continuing for 6-12 weeks postpartum.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"443","duplicate_group_id":"exact-4a2e78b58270","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"c4c87b63fda7bf54cd93","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":635,"source_qid":"443"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"c4c87b63fda7bf54cd93","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":635,"source_qid":"443","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 34-year-old pregnant woman presents to your office for evaluation at 12 weeks gestation. Her obstetrical history is significant for 2 miscarriages in previous pregnancies, for which she underwent assessment and was found to have\nantiphospholipid syndrome. She is currently on aspirin. Which one of the following would be the next best step in management?","options":{"A":"Do nothing, as aspirin alone is adequate.","B":"Start her on prophylactic dose of low molecular weight heparin.","C":"Start her on warfarin.","D":"Start her on therapeutic dose of low molecular weight heparin","E":"Arrange for elective abortion."},"source_answer":"B","source_explanation":"For women with laboratory-proven criteria for antiphospholipid antibody syndrome and one or more miscarriages after 10 weeks gestation, combined therapy with low-dose aspirin (50 to 100 mg per day) and prophylactic dose of low molecular\nweight heparin (LMWH) upon confirmation of intrauterine pregnancy is recommended. Therefore, addition of 