Acute systemic reactions following an intravenous heparin bolus
If heparin-induced HIT is suspected, the first step is to discontinue and avoid all heparin products immediately. Even small doses for catheter flushing should be avoided.
(Option A) HIT is not caused by pneumatic compression; therefore, its discontinuation has no benefit in management of this patient. 
(Option B) Warfarin should be avoided in such patients because it can lead to microthrombosis. Interestingly, patients with HIT have an INR of above 4. Warfarin can be started once the platelet count is back to normal. If warfarin has already been
started, vitamin K should be given.
(Option D) Once a Doppler ultrasound has confirms the diagnosis of DVT, venography is not required as an extra measure unless some surgical intervention is planned and an accurate venous map is required.
(Option E) Platelet transfusion should be avoided in HIT, as it may increase the thrombogenic effect. Guidelines from the American College of Chest Physicians suggest limiting platelet transfusions to patients with severe thrombocytopenia, who are
experiencing bleeding or undergoing an invasive procedure with a high risk of bleeding.
Once HIT occurs, alternatives to heparin are direct thrombin inhibitors (DTIs) such as argatroban and the indirect factor Xa inhibitor fondaparinux (Arixtra®).',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"671","duplicate_group_id":"exact-df99cbdd5630","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e2a27c3f2d17771ad8c9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":636,"source_qid":"671"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
