* WCC is not very reliable for differentiating the causative organism in meningtis. A CSF WCC of 5-100 can be seen in early bacterial meningitis, viral meningitis, TB meningitis and fungal meningitis.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"1130","duplicate_group_id":"exact-6bd2ade9eddc","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f5f1e90693f52e529ede","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":676,"source_qid":"1130"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"f5f1e90693f52e529ede","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":676,"source_qid":"1130","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 5-year-old boy is brought to the emergency department with lethargy and a fever. On examination, he has neck stiffness. With meningitis as the most likely diagnosis, a lumbar puncture is performed, the result of which is as follows:\nOpening pressure: 45mmH2O (5-20)\nAppearance: cloudy\nProtein: 1.2g/L (0.18-0.45)\nGlucose: 1.5mmol/L (2.5-3.5)\nWCC: 900/mm3 (<3) neutrophil predominance\nThe child is started on intravenous cefotaxime. Which one of the following should be considered as the most appropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"Oral paracetamol.","B":"Aspirin.","C":"Intravenous dexamethasone.","D":"Acyclovir.","E":"CT scan of the head."},"source_answer":"C","source_explanation":"If possible, an LP should be performed prior to starting antibiotics in suspected cases of meningitis. This child has a CSF analysis consistent with the diagnosis of bacterial meningitis. High protein, low glucose and increased WCC with 