mily history), as well as in\nindividuals with probable ischemia and otherwise negative workup. A full blood exam should also be obtained to screen for conditions such as polycythemia vera and essential thrombocythemia.\nOf the options, the most important initial test to consider is Duplex Doppler ultrasonography of carotid arteries since most visual losses are due to carotid artery stenoses. Absence of carotid bruit does not exclude the possibility of carotid stenosis\nas the most likely cause of retinal ischemia in this patient.\n(Option A) CT scan of the brain can be considered after CGA and carotid stenosis are excluded as the possible causes of the presentation.\n(Option B) As mentioned earlier, EEG is not used routinely for evaluation of a patient with MTVL. \n(Option C) Brain imaging (MRI) is indicated in older patients with clues to posterior circulation insufficiency.\n(Option E) Echocardiography is considered when CGA and carotid stenosis as the most common causes of TVL are excluded.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","diabetes","hypertension","screen","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"65f3b1e1fa29b076dde5a5669da933f7e57401b1","duplicate_group_id":"exact-65f3b1e1fa29","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"03d276b2e7f2a837eb8f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":716,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answe